= Client-server model — Technical =

Client-server systems can be stateful or stateless, synchronous or asynchronous, and can include intermediaries such as proxies, gateways, caches, and load balancers. Role boundaries are defined by interaction behavior rather than device class.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* client/server role ≠ permanent machine identity
* client-server ≠ centralized system necessarily
* server ≠ physical server hardware necessarily

== References ==
* Andrew S. Tanenbaum and Maarten van Steen, ''Distributed Systems'', client-server architectural model.
* W3C, ''Architecture of the World Wide Web, Volume One'', user-agent and origin-server interaction model.
